  (label "5V_MAIN" (at 466.0 236.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 22c100fa-61d7-52e4-8127-333e2999a477)
  )
  (text "BOSCH WIRING (terminal diagram 0 462 YU4 15D, decisions log sec.18). The ECU has NO permanent battery feed: pin 71 (ignition) wakes it,\npin 50 closes the main relay, and the relay's contact feeds pins 04/06, the board's only supply. Q-WAKE closes the relay in hardware from pin 71,\nso the board can come up at all; the MCU then holds RLY_MAIN through the after-run (stop, save fault memory) and releases it last.\n\nPIN 50 HAS A TVS, NOT A FLYBACK DIODE. Its coil sits on Term. 30, always live. A diode from the drain to VBAT_PROT powered the board THROUGH THE COIL\nwith the relay open: 22.8 mA in the coil (2.7x its release current) and the board at 9.1 V (main_relay.cir part B). The relay could never drop out.\nBosch marks pin 50 'not equipped with freewheeling diode'. The buzzer relay keeps its diode: its coil is on the main-relay line and dies with VBAT_PROT.\n\nNO TRIP LOOP. It had no Bosch pin. The overspeed trip module (external) opens the main relay's coil feed, which drops the board with everything else.\nPin 21 is the WATER-IN-FUEL input, active high from the main-relay line through the sensor's switch, open (reads inactive) with no water." (at 40.0 340.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left))
    (uuid ad2bb6ad-dddd-5c56-8179-d5d3c84db683)
  )
  (text "THE EIGHT SWITCH INPUTS ARE NPN BUFFERS, NOT CLAMPS (22 Sep 2026, LOWV-CLAMP). The 47k/68k/3.0 V-zener front end needed a clamp that conducts CONTINUOUSLY over 6-40 V, and none\nfits the pad's ratings: a 3.0 V zener leaks at uA (soft knee), a rail clamp parks the pad at 3.9 V, a shunt reference draws 35 uA of bias the cranking-dip input cannot supply.\nHere the pad sees only its own 10k pull-up or a saturated PMBT3904-Q. Checked at the WORST corner, not typical: hFE 30 at -40 C still pulls the pad to 0.03 V from a 6 V input;\na typical part at 125 C does not turn on below 1.3 V. 10k input resistors give 1.1 mA of contact wetting current at 12 V.\n\nLOGIC IS INVERTED -- pad LOW = input active (contact-to-ground channels: contact OPEN). FAILURE MODES, for firmware plausibility checks: transistor open or pull-up shorted\n-> pad stuck HIGH (reads inactive); C-E short -> pad stuck LOW (reads active). One polarity cannot make every channel fail safe; the safe state per channel belongs in the\nfirmware spec. The trip loop keeps its clamped ANALOG front end: its healthy band is the clamp level (LOWV-CLAMP residual)." (at 40.0 392.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left))
    (uuid 391565c7-4ab6-587b-ac90-a70143f59433)
  )
